WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.960
<i>As the three-way battle continues,</i>

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.750
<i>Hong exudes bacteria in 
order to protect Annex 1.</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.740
<i>No. 3 Division is forced to retreat.</i>

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.030
Everyone, retreat!

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.400
<i>But Alexander goes in alone 
on a suicide mission</i>

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.200
<i>for the sleeping princess 
who awaits his return.</i>

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.960
<i>His reckless act causes severe 
damage to No. 4 Division.</i>

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.650
Hong-chan.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.980
Y-Yes?

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.500
As soon as we're done treating 
Xi-san and the others,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.420
we'll follow the Second.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.420
You stay here.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.660
There's plenty of food.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.000
Use as much of the drug as you can

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.410
without burning yourself out 
to keep the bacteria going.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.220
O-Okay...

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.550
Um...

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.860
You're right.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.370
Huh? What is it, Hong?

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.150
You're not getting any ideas in that 
pretty little head of yours, are you?

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:12.880
Huh?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.510
You did everything you could to protect us.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.910
So we did everything we could to protect you.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.480
That's all there is to it.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.600
It's going to take time to treat them.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.790
We're gonna be a little late.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:33.890
The First and Second were cut 
off from Captain Komachi.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.000
I hope the terraformars haven't 
split them up and captured them.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.510
Contact Unit 1 and Unit 2.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.540
Okay.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:21.490
Weapons and 
Techniques

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.810
<i>Hand over the First and Second.</i>

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.350
<i>Or we'll hit you with that missile.</i>

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.690
Doesn't No. 4 Division's way of doing 
things piss you off, Michelle-san?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.370
They're after the two of us,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.590
so how can you be so calm?

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.230
It's the difference in our level of resolve.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.170
No. 4 Division's stupid 
plans don't matter to me.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.130
I came here with too much resolve.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:03:59.990
Resolve?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.500
I also...

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.390
Wh-What?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:13.890
What is it?

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.520
L-Look!

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.470
Michelle.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:42.910
Michelle?

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.370
Paraponera...

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.880
You up, Captain?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.630
Um, Captain...

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.700
I'm sorry for acting alone.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:32.950
You've got that right.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.990
Every single division is like that.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.930
Well, you saved me when I needed it.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:38.980
Thanks.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.180
Is this everyone?

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.720
Yeah.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.230
My son's dead.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.410
The fool.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.090
No matter how much it frustrated him,

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:54.370
no matter how close we were to the Annex 1...

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:58.320
Even if the whole situation was insane...

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.340
It's a violation of orders to die, right?

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.190
Now...

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.650
I have to make the vaccine, 
even if it kills me!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.180
Captain...

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.820
I'll tell you what's going on, 
and everything I know.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.190
The bacteria-type M.O. Operation 
that was performed on that girl...

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.220
That was probably Branch Office 4's 
independently-developed technology.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.130
A humanoid bioweapon...

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.070
That's right.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.220
As long as it can get close to the target,

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.960
it can commit assassination 
or terrorism at will.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.550
The rest of them have 
also probably undergone

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.760
some strange, perverted surgeries 
that are different to ours.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.630
Even in their normal forms they had power

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.980
almost equivalent to 
after they'd transformed.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.150
But that means that can't 
function in everyday life.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.020
I would imagine that just

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.860
spending a night in the same 
room as the bacteria type

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.450
would be enough to get sick.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.420
Someone with sharpened 
senses wouldn't be able to

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:16.080
enjoy smells or music that 
were intended for humans.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.450
Th-Then they're...

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.810
Yes.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:23.750
To gain that power, 
they've abandoned our one hope:

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.860
a normal life once we've returned to Earth.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.500
They're strong.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.390
They've made enemies of 
 all the other divisions,

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.340
and even sacrificed their own futures.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.420
Do they want those two so badly?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.980
Probably.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.520
Those two were born with Mosaic Organs.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.740
XO Davis was a legitimate miracle.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.780
Not artificially created.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.280
But Hizamaru Akari is another matter.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.270
He was clearly artificially created.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.790
There must be a way to cause Mosaic 
Organs to become inheritable.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.330
If it's possible to create a 
human who is sure to successfully

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.830
undergo the M.O. surgery,

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.710
that technology could exist 
in 20 years at the latest.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.470
An army of a hundred crab soldiers!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.430
A hundreds spies who can control electricity.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.390
You could even make a politician 
who's immune to poison.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.770
Of course, the medical possibilities 
are limitless, as well.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.510
If you could get a monopoly on it, 
you would become incredibly rich.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.550
You could be stronger than any other country!

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.990
Of course they want it.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.810
We'll follow Akari and Michelle.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.660
We'll save the two of them 
before No. 4 Division acts.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.760
Yes, sir.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.270
Roger, Captain.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.070
It's not just No. 4 Division that wants them.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.960
We need to hurry.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:06.460
Captured.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.070
You're a bullet ant.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.320
Paraponera, yes?

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.890
M.A.R.S. Ranking #6.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.940
Hizamaru Akari

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.940
Surgery Base: Eumeta Japonica

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.940
M.A.R.S. Ranking #6

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.420
Bagworm Moth.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.970
Hizamaru Akari.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.960
Please just let me catch you 
more easily than I expect to.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.250
The name's Michelle K. Davis.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:51.940
I'm taking that ability back.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.190
What's wrong, Akari?

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:58.570
Are you worried I'll lose my cool 
in the face of my father's ability?

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.380
Thanks.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.580
I've been ready for this ever since 
I learned the terraformars

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.210
could steal our abilities.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.140
I'm extremely calm.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.670
But very pissed.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.010
Akari!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:16.880
Right!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.020
Don't underestimate the threads of a bagworm!

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.180
Michelle-san, follow the plan!

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.040
Were you there the whole time, Michelle?

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:43.030
Do you like ants?

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.410
Kinda!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.240
You just happen to have arms that look like his.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.500
I have no attachment to you.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.380
I'm just going to stop you so 
you can't follow my friends.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.160
I'm just going to kill you, 
because you're a terraformar!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.230
<i>I can feel her blows through the threads.</i>

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.030
<i>They're heavy...</i>

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.700
<i>She's steeled herself for this all week?</i>

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.280
<i>She's calm?</i>

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.260
<i>She has no attachment?</i>

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.000
<i>Then why are they so heavy?</i>

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.790
But did you know, Michelle?

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.350
Ants...

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.090
This is the end for you.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.510
Out of all the insects, they're...

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.260
Even a Paraponera can't break my threads!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.340
Michelle-san, go!

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:47.850
They're the...

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.220
They're the...

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.030
They're the strongest.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.710
But a little of it 
should've gotten into him...

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:17.190
Michelle-san's camponotus saundersi 
exploding bodily fluids!

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.570
What's wrong?

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.610
You can't break through, can you?

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.500
Sorry, but I'm not a brute-force type like Michelle-san!

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.830
I'll lock you down

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.290
and bury you underground!

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.160
The threads!

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>Paraponera Type Terraformar</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>The Paraponera is capable of lifting up to 100 times its own weight and has a neurotoxin as strong as a giant hornet.</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>It is the strongest ant in history, and attacks even humans and other animals.</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>Due to its fierce nature, and the fact that its bite feels like being struck by a gunshot,</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>it was given the name "bullet ant."</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.950
<b>This ability originally belonged to Michelle's father, Donatello K. Davis.</b>

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.980
What?

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:50.050
You want me, too?

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.280
You want these threads?

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.840
But you know, Paraponera,

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.690
I'm too scared to turn around.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.580
'Cause now she's really mad.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.110
Round two, assholes.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.230
If you want it, try to capture me.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.900
The bagworm threads are melting?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.150
<i>Acid?</i>

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:29.030
<i>Carabus blaptoides?</i>

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.470
Akari, get it in your 
eyes and you'll go blind!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.560
Seriously?

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.260
That ain't good!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.940
So you decided your powers give

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:19.100
you an advantage over me, rather than him?

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:21.040
Just what I was hoping for!

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.100
I see.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.530
So you can melt my threads at will, huh?

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:41.040
Lately I've just been this handy guy who 
can spin thread, and it's making me sad.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:45.170
If I can't use my threads, 
I'll just have to crush you.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.850
<i>There're no openings!</i>

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.900
He's emitting acid from his feet?

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.290
No!

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.960
First round... I win!

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.470
<i>They feel no pain!</i>

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:53.280
<i>That's not... cowardice.</i>

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.850
<i>He's willing to do what it takes to win.</i>

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.000
<i>Hizamaru-kun!</i>

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.550
<i>Hizamaru-kun was shot!</i>

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:11.880
<i>The terraformars are about to take him!</i>

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.120
Incoming transmission. It's Unit 2.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:17.130
<i>We almost certainly will not 
be able to recover the body.</i>

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.250
<i>That's bad, right?</i>

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:22.830
Because of Hizamaru-kun we 
have a missile locked on us,

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.980
and I've been forced to drive so 
dangerously that I'm about to throw up.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:27.990
I just can't take it anymore!

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.110
Please fire!

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.300
Hizamaru-kun and Michelle-san are fighting

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.640
directly in between Units 1 and 2.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:39.070
Throw down some firepower and just 
kill them and the terraformars.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:42.540
Just please make sure I survive!

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.310
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.840
<i>Once they're dead the terraformars 
will come after me!</i>

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:49.760
<i>I don't want to die! Save me!</i>

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:52.050
So Rank 98 betrayed them?

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:55.210
Maybe that's what you can 
expect from a non-combatant

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.010
who's caught up in all this.

00:17:57.390 --> 00:18:00.260
Units 1 and 2 are indeed in 
the position she describes.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:01.700
Let's do it.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.300
Firing.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:19.530
No. 4 Division is afraid of Akari and 
I being taken by the terraformars

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.250
so they can't recover 
any parts of our bodies,

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.540
and No. 1 and No. 2

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.410
Divisions meeting up with Joseph 
and the rest of No. 6 Division

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.640
and coming back to kill them all.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.860
We can't use our radios,

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:33.460
so we'll send up a smoke signal to 
alert No. 6 Division to our peril.

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:35.660
For that, we have them shoot the missile.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.580
So you pretend to betray us.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:39.380
I-I'll try it!

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.470
Y-Yaeko!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.580
When you think I'm about 
to lose, follow the plan!

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.520
We'll get rid of one of 
No. 4 Division's missiles, too!

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:48.950
Right!

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.590
I believe in you, Alex!

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.190
Leave it to me, Yaeko.

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:01.780
I'll shoot it through and 
use that as a smoke signal!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.120
I'm gonna come back as a ghost and haunt you!

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:39.740
It didn't go off?

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:48.250
We wasted their missile, but we 
didn't get our smoke signal.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:49.540
It failed?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.090
Setting second round.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:01.800
Wait!

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:05.340
Did it go off course and miss the target?

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:06.760
Why?

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.310
Rank 7? What did he do?

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:17.660
<i>It was far too narrow a tightrope</i>

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:20.240
<i>they had to cross for it 
to even be called a plan.</i>

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:24.080
<i>If Liu didn't fire the missile...</i>

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:28.670
<i>If the missile hit Unit 2, where Yaeko was...</i>

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:32.410
<i>If the missile exploded...</i>

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:37.330
<i>It was a very narrow thread of 
hope that they had to connect,</i>

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.510
<i>that threatened to break at any moment!</i>

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:41.880
<i>But...</i>

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:43.920
Thank you...

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.840
Whoever you were.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.750
A fallen companion from another 
land was there to help!

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.850
If I've got this...

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.870
I can fight just one more round!

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:04.400
<i>So Rank 7 knew that we'd fire 
without hesitation if we had to?</i>

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:07.020
<i>The reason they only destroyed 
the launcher was a feint</i>

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:09.200
<i>to make us think the missiles 
themselves were still safe!</i>

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:11.380
<i>And the weapon that cut them apart...</i>

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:16.080
<i>They'd already taken out the warhead's 
explosives and put that weapon in instead?</i>

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.880
<i>But the center of gravity shifted...</i>

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:21.130
<i>So that weapon was...</i>

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.440
I don't know who you are,

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:27.500
but I've received your hopes.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:32.310
A weapon whose location only I 
can determine, with my moth powers...

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:38.020
<i>It was a special weapon that Rank 7 
sacrificed himself to give to Rank 6.</i>

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.020
If you're using guns...

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.320
Then I'll use a weapon, too!

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:49.050
<i>The anti-terraformar vibro-ninja-blade!</i>

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.490
<i>Known as...</i>

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.890
<b>Hizamaru</b>

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:55.710
<i>Hizamaru!</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.940
First Day

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:39.810
Nighty-night, Paraponera.
